        <briefdescription>
<para>Non-equality operator for containers. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Constructs an <computeroutput>ne_</computeroutput> comparator object from the two container operands and returns it. The comparator evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the containers are not equal in content or order.</para>
<para>The operator is enabled only for types recognised as containers by the framework&apos;s type traits.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The left-hand container type, constrained to recognised container types. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The right-hand container type, constrained to recognised container types.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The left hand side container operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The right hand side container operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A comparator object that evaluates to true if the containers are not equal. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
