    <briefdescription>
<para>Overloaded operators for container comparison. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Within test cases, overloaded operators support direct and expressive comparison of standard containers, such as vectors and strings. These operators enable clear, concise assertions when verifying equality or inequality of container contents.</para>
<para>In addition to generic operators, specialised equality and inequality operators are available for container types where dedicated handling improves correctness or efficiency, while preserving modern C++ semantics.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Examples</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;vector&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>containers<sp/>with<sp/>operators&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">using<sp/>namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt::operators;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}<sp/>==<sp/>std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>})</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}<sp/>==<sp/>vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>3<sp/>}<sp/>!=<sp/>std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>4<sp/>})</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>3<sp/>}<sp/>!=<sp/>vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>4<sp/>}&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
